{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '177,219p;240,310p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '177,195p;245,286p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '21,31p;56,75p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '4,13p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,78p;117,132p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-claude.md | head -130; rg -n 'D560|D606|D358|D424' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | rg '\"'^.*##'\"'; nl -ba README.md | sed -n '101,140p'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js | sed -n '254,266p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Council P: Claude's position, written before reading Codex's\n     2\t\n     3\t## The system (poc-v118), end to end\n     4\t1. **Sources.** A batch harvest toolchain (`poc/corpus/README.md`; `poc/corpus/scripts/harvest_*.py`: Google News, GDELT, EDGAR,\n     5\t   official notices, company blogs) → `assemble.py` → `freeze_window.sh` → `clean_pages.py` (D351). It is run by hand per window;\n     6\t   there is no scheduler. The last harvested window is NVDA 07-01..10-27 (`items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite`).\n     7\t2. **Dispatch** (`dispatch.py`): each item validated, numbered and routed, in order.\n     8\t3. **Extraction** (`extraction.py`, `gpt-6-luna`, v74i, low effort; one call per article): reads the questions open at day start,\n     9\t   files quoted evidence under them, proposes new questions.\n    10\t4. **Matching and writing** (`views/jev_matching.py`, Jev 1.14 with the collision judge; `views/writing.py`): open, merge or skip a\n    11\t   candidate; repeat, replacement or new for evidence; append-only SQLite.\n    12\t5. **Judging** (`views/judging.py`, judging-v7): once a day, the questions whose evidence changed get a rung on their ladder, with\n    13\t   citations.\n    14\t6. **Pull mode** (`pull.py`): a question closes at its rung on its due day.\n    15\t7. **Driver** (`scripts/replay.py`): days in order over a frozen items database; it resumes after a store's last completed day\n    16\t   (`src/hivemind/replay.py:62`), so a store can be extended.\n    17\t8. **Serving:** HTTP API, MCP server, the page (Thesis Library, Explore Ideas) and the Idea call (`poc-v118-idea`, three calls). They\n    18\t   serve the sealed `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828` ledger, built by the older `poc-v34` (README, \"Local requirements\";\n    19\t   DECISIONS §13). **No analyst has seen poc-v118's own output on the page.**\n    20\t\n    21\t## Performance (measured)\n    22\t- **Release comparison** (07-01..09-20, 82 days, about 1,884 articles, 3 draws; `2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:32-41`):\n    23\t  old serves 10 of 32 key matters (\"served\" = a covering question rated worth tracking and supported, plan v12 item 5); the new\n    24\t  system 2–3. Each old draw cost $8.60–$9.83 (about $0.11 a day) and took under three hours of wall clock for 82 days; no stop.\n    25\t- **Answer quality:** among worth-tracking questions in the 5 stored draws, 24 answers were rejected by both blind readers\n    26\t  (`2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md`): overlapping amounts added, a figure of another scope taken as the answer, unsupported\n    27\t  adjustments, talks taken as likely completion. About 16 of 24 step off a reference rung the judge itself named.\n    28\t- **Frozen ruler** (14 days, judgement at 07-14): poc-v116 53/57 against poc-v108 45/57, three draws (`CURRENT_STATE.md:134`).\n    29\t  poc-v118 itself cannot be scored by the seeded scorer (README, \"Run the pipeline\").\n    30\t- **Never measured:** a second company; live latency; a window past 09-20 for poc-v118; a human analyst's read of its output (the\n    31\t  pilot deck has waited on Alex since D560); evidence growth over months (open defect 7, D358 stopped the v34 run on bloat).\n    32\t\n    33\t## Readiness for a production test\n    34\t| Requirement | State | Evidence |\n    35\t|---|---|---|\n    36\t| New articles each day | Partly: tools exist, run by hand per window, no schedule; corpus ends 10-27 | `poc/corpus/README.md` |\n    37\t| The pipeline run each day on a continuing store | Partly: replay resumes a store; a daily wrapper and an items database that grows are not built | `src/hivemind/replay.py:62` |\n    38\t| Its store served to the page, API and MCP | Partly: one-edit swap documented; serving-while-writing proofs were built for the new system's writer (D594–D603), and a restart is Alex's | README \"Switching the served data\"; `OPERATING-CONTRACT.md` |\n    39\t| Cost cap and monitoring | Partly: `--cap` per run, not hard; cost is small (about $0.11/day for one company) | README \"Run the pipeline\" |\n    40\t| Quality accepted | No: not accepted end to end; 10 of 32 matters; no human read | `CURRENT_STATE.md:133` |\n    41\t| Hosting | Host only: Docker has no outbound model calls under the VPN | AGENTS §9 |\n    42\t\n    43\t**Verdict: NOT READY for a live production test today; READY for a shadow forward test now.** The pipeline is complete and stable\n    44\tover 82 days, cheap, and has never stopped; what is missing is (a) a daily feed and wrapper, engineering of a few days, and (b) any\n    45\thuman read of what it gives an analyst.\n    46\t\n    47\t**Recommendation and one test.** Run poc-v118 forward from one old draw's 09-20 store over the unseen 09-21..10-27 articles (already\n    48\tharvested; about $3 for one draw at old's rate, Alex's money since D439 has $0), serve that store locally on the page, and have Alex\n    49\tread it for half an hour: is this something an analyst would use? It tests the two things never tested (fresh articles after the\n    50\tdesign's window, and the product page showing poc-v118's output) and decides whether the daily-feed engineering is worth building.\n3783:## D358 · 2026-10-28 (carried 2026-11-04) · The three-month run stops at 2026-08-28 and is sealed; evidence bloat is the next problem to solve\n4698:## D424 · 2026-11-10 · The writer keeps giving a \"later version\" the older record's questions; the fix is closed without a change\n7047:## D560 · 2026-11-15 · Reflection council (Alex's request): the goal, the measuring method and the way through; a pilot of Alex's own product-level review is prepared at $0; the role of the six lines is put to him (council consensus)\n8060:## D606 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 148): the items on Alex's page that D439 permits are decided reversibly; next, a $0 audit of the postponed-event class\n8091:## D607 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 149): D606's postponement reading is reversed provisionally; the postponement repair route closes; next, a $0 audit of the shared fiscal-year note\n9293:## D662 · 2026-11-17 · Reflection council 9 (Alex's request): the work drifted from D560's agreed way out; hold the listed work and put Deck 1 to Alex first (council consensus)\n   101\t### Switching the served data\n   102\t\n   103\tThe page build, the two services and Compose each carry the same two defaults: the thesis ledger (`views.sqlite`) and the items database the ledger's input ids come from. Swap both together; a ledger whose items are missing shows evidence without titles or sources. Serve a copy of a ledger a run may still write (`snapshot.sh` in a run folder makes one with SQLite's backup API), never the file the run writes. The places that name the defaults, all changed in one edit:\n   104\t\n   105\t| Place | What to change |\n   106\t|---|---|\n   107\t| `scripts/mock_build.py` | `--ledger` and `--items` defaults, then `python3 scripts/mock_build.py` rebuilds `poc/mock/index.html` |\n   108\t| `scripts/hivemind_api.py` | `--views` and `--items` defaults |\n   109\t| `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` | `--views` and `--items` defaults |\n   110\t| `docker-compose.yml` | the `/data/ledger` and `/data/items/items-window.sqlite` volumes of both services |\n   111\t| This README and `poc/ui/README.md` | the default paths named in the table above and in the build description |\n   112\t| `tests/test_ui_bundles.py` | `SERVED_VIEWS` and `SERVED_GROUPS`, the served library's thesis and group counts |\n   113\t\n   114\tThen restart the API in a new dated service folder (below) so the search index is built for the new ledger. The current default, `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828`, is the three-month NVDA run (`poc-v34`, extraction v18) stopped and sealed at 2026-08-28 on evidence bloat (D358); its folder README names the one empty thesis removed.\n   115\t\n   116\t## Run the service for testing\n   117\t\n   118\tRun test services on the host. Start with read-only browsing and lexical search, which need no model or embedding calls. In the same shell where `repo` names the checkout, create a fresh dated run directory for the log, PID and derived files:\n   119\t\n   120\t```sh\n   121\tservice_run=$(mktemp -d \"$repo/poc/data/service-$(date +%F)-XXXXXX\")\n   122\tnohup python3 \"$repo/scripts/hivemind_api.py\" --port 8788 \\\n   123\t  --lexical --config '' \\\n   124\t  --index \"$service_run/search-index.sqlite\" \\\n   125\t  --archive \"$service_run/idea-archive.sqlite\" \\\n   126\t  > \"$service_run/api.log\" 2>&1 &\n   127\tprintf '%s\\n' \"$!\" > \"$service_run/api.pid\"\n   128\tcurl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8788/days\n   129\t```\n   130\t\n   131\t`/days` returns the first and last completed ledger day. See the log if startup is not ready. To enable Idea submission and semantic search, stop this instance and start the same command without `--lexical --config ''`. That selects the default Idea configuration above and can call the embedding and language models. Exact archived requests can replay without another model call; changed requests can incur cost.\n   132\t\n   133\tThe app calls `http://127.0.0.1:8788`; its host may override this with `<body data-api=\"…\">`. `/library` returns the dated snapshot. `--views` and `--items` select other source databases; `--index`, `--archive` and `--config` select derived storage and configuration. Stop only the API instance you started:\n   134\t\n   135\t```sh\n   136\tkill \"$(cat \"$service_run/api.pid\")\"\n   137\t```\n   138\t\n   139\tFor an agent, `scripts/hivemind_mcp.py` defaults to stdio. Use `--transport streamable-http --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8789` to serve `/mcp`, and `--lexical` for model-free reads. The [service contract](docs/poc/service.md) lists the tools and historical-read rules.\n   140\t\n   254\t    async function loadLibrary() {\n   255\t      try {\n   256\t        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\n   257\t        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Service returned ${response.status}`);\n   258\t        const next = fromBundles(await response.json());\n   259\t        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\n   260\t          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\n   261\t        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\n   262\t        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\n   263\t        data = next;\n   264\t      } catch {\n   265\t        // Keep the displayed snapshot when the optional live read is unavailable.\n   266\t      }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '177,219p;240,310p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_api.py | sed -n '177,195p;245,286p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind_mcp.py | sed -n '21,31p;56,75p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md | sed -n '4,13p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,78p;117,132p'\"","aggregated_output":"   177\t                        state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {label} is gone'\n   178\t                        break\n   179\t            return dict(state)\n   180\t\n   181\t    def claim_launcher(self, label, lock_handle):\n   182\t        \"\"\"One step under the ledger's lock (council mo, D449): stop the ledger if any registered launcher's lock is free; try the\n   183\t        launcher's own lock without blocking (False: another launch of this label is running); if this label is still registered once\n   184\t        its lock is held, the previous launcher died without removing its entry, so the ledger stops; then register. The stop gate's\n   185\t        probe takes the same lock, so no send can see a stale entry as alive while a new launcher takes its lock.\"\"\"\n   186\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   187\t            launchers = state.setdefault('launchers', {})\n   188\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   189\t                for other, lock_path in sorted(launchers.items()):\n   190\t                    if lock_is_free(lock_path):\n   191\t                        state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {other} is gone'\n   192\t                        break\n   193\t            try:\n   194\t                fcntl.flock(lock_handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n   195\t            except BlockingIOError:\n   196\t                return False\n   197\t            if label in launchers and not state.get('stopped'):\n   198\t                state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, f'the launcher of {label} is gone'\n   199\t            launchers[label] = os.path.abspath(lock_handle.name)\n   200\t            return True\n   201\t\n   202\t    def register_launcher(self, label, lock_path):\n   203\t        \"\"\"Register a launcher's lock path (tests and proofs; a launcher uses `claim_launcher`).\"\"\"\n   204\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   205\t            state.setdefault('launchers', {})[label] = str(lock_path)\n   206\t\n   207\t    def remove_launcher(self, label):\n   208\t        \"\"\"Called by a launcher on a normal end, before it releases its lock.\"\"\"\n   209\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   210\t            (state.get('launchers') or {}).pop(label, None)\n   211\t\n   212\t    def stop(self, reason):\n   213\t        \"\"\"A stop any component records: every later reservation is refused.\"\"\"\n   214\t        with self._locked() as state:\n   215\t            if not state.get('stopped'):\n   216\t                state['stopped'], state['stop_reason'] = True, reason\n   217\t\n   218\t    def read(self):\n   219\t        with open(self.lock_path, 'a+') as lock:\n   240\tdef llm_cost(response, request):\n   241\t    \"\"\"The answer's cost by `model.call`'s formula; None (settled at the reservation) unless the counts are whole, nonnegative numbers\n   242\t    with some input.\"\"\"\n   243\t    usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   244\t    if not isinstance(usage, dict):\n   245\t        return None\n   246\t    tokens_in, tokens_out = usage.get('prompt_tokens'), usage.get('completion_tokens')\n   247\t    details = usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}\n   248\t    cached = (details.get('cached_tokens') or 0) if isinstance(details, dict) else None\n   249\t    if not (whole(tokens_in) and whole(tokens_out) and whole(cached)) or tokens_in == 0:\n   250\t        return None\n   251\t    price_in, price_out = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   252\t    cached = min(tokens_in, cached)\n   253\t    return (tokens_in - cached) / 1e6 * price_in + cached / 1e6 * price_in * model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + tokens_out / 1e6 * price_out\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef jev_estimate(request):\n   257\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES[request['model']]\n   258\t    tokens_in = 2 * len(json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')) + 4096\n   259\t    return jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens_in * price_in / 1e6\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\n   307\t            actual = jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6\n   308\t        else:\n   309\t            actual = estimate                       # usage missing, invalid, or zero for a nonempty request: the whole reservation\n   310\t        self.ledger.settle(estimate, actual, kind='jev', tokens=tokens if isinstance(tokens, int) else None)\n   177\t        def prepare(db):\n   178\t            \"\"\"The store's date refusals, before any header (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3): a first-day store, and a date after the last\n   179\t            completed day. A malformed body or a missing configuration is answered in the stream, as before (D281).\"\"\"\n   180\t            try:\n   181\t                as_of = request_body().get('as_of') or None\n   182\t            except (KeyError, ValueError):\n   183\t                as_of = None                          # the body's own error is raised by `work`, in the stream\n   184\t            service.resolve_bound(db.ledger, as_of)\n   185\t\n   186\t        def work(db, on_progress=None):\n   187\t            body = request_body()\n   188\t            if CFG is None:\n   189\t                raise config.ConfigError('the server was started without --config, so it cannot read ideas')\n   190\t            return idea.read_idea(db.ledger, db.index, db.items, db.archive, CFG, body['text'], body.get('as_of') or None,\n   191\t                                  int(body.get('k') or 10), aliases=ALIASES, semantic=SEMANTIC, bundles=body.get('bundles', True) is not False,\n   192\t                                  on_progress=on_progress)\n   193\t        accepted = [part.split(';', 1)[0].strip() for part in self.headers.get('Accept', '').split(',')]\n   194\t        if parts == ['ideas'] and 'application/x-ndjson' in accepted:\n   195\t            self._stream_answer(work, prepare)\n   245\tdef index_at_start(embed=None):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The search index built at start to the last completed day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4a); on a first-day store nothing is\n   247\t    built, and search stays lexical until the service is restarted after a day completes. Returns the line the server prints.\"\"\"\n   248\t    with Connections() as db:\n   249\t        try:\n   250\t            embedded, unchanged, tokens, error = search.ensure_index(db.ledger, db.index, **({'embed': embed} if embed else {}))\n   251\t        except service.FirstDayNotCompleted:\n   252\t            return \"index: not built, the store's first day has not completed; search is lexical until a restart after it completes\"\n   253\t    return f'index: {embedded} views embedded, {unchanged} unchanged, {tokens} tokens' + (f'; embedding stopped ({error}): search runs lexical until the rest is built' if error else '')\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef main():\n   257\t    global ALIASES, CFG, SEMANTIC\n   258\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   259\t    parser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\n   260\t    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'), help='the items database, for source titles in the idea card')\n   261\t    parser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\n   262\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'idea-archive.sqlite'), help='where idea model calls are archived for replay')\n   263\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118-idea.json'), help='the config whose idea settings name the mapping and final assessment models and prompts')\n   264\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n   265\t    parser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\n   266\t    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8788)\n   267\t    parser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\n   268\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n   269\t    PATHS.update(views=args.views, items=args.items, index=args.index, archive=args.archive)\n   270\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.archive)), exist_ok=True)\n   271\t    ALIASES = search.object_aliases(args.universe)\n   272\t    CFG = config.load(args.config) if args.config and os.path.exists(args.config) else None\n   273\t    SEMANTIC = not args.lexical\n   274\t    if not os.path.exists(args.items):\n   275\t        print(f'items database not found ({args.items}): idea cards name sources by input id', flush=True)\n   276\t    if CFG is None:\n   277\t        print('no config: GET routes only, POST /ideas answers 502', flush=True)\n   278\t    else:\n   279\t        print(f'config {CFG.version}: ideas read by {CFG.idea.model} ({CFG.idea.prompt_version}, effort {CFG.idea.reasoning_effort}); archive {os.path.basename(args.archive)}', flush=True)\n   280\t        if CFG.idea_summary is not None:\n   281\t            print(f'analyst summary: {CFG.idea_summary.model} ({CFG.idea_summary.prompt_version}, effort {CFG.idea_summary.reasoning_effort})', flush=True)\n   282\t    if args.lexical:\n   283\t        print('--lexical: no embedding; every search answers in lexical mode', flush=True)\n   284\t    else:\n   285\t        print(index_at_start(), flush=True)\n   286\t    print(f'hivemind api on http://{args.host}:{args.port}  ledger {os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(args.views))}/{os.path.basename(args.views)}  index {os.path.basename(args.index)}', flush=True)\n    21\tparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    22\tparser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\n    23\tparser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\n    24\tparser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    25\tparser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    26\tparser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\n    27\tparser.add_argument('--transport', choices=['stdio', 'streamable-http'], default='stdio', help='stdio for a local agent; streamable-http to serve /mcp over HTTP (Docker)')\n    28\tparser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\n    29\tparser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8789)\n    30\tARGS = parser.parse_args()\n    31\tALIASES = search_module.object_aliases(ARGS.universe)\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\tdef start_objects():\n    59\t    \"\"\"The object list for the server's instructions, computed once at start and labelled with its day; every tool reads the current\n    60\t    last completed day. Start-up indexing embeds only views visible at the last completed day, and none on a first-day store (row 4a).\"\"\"\n    61\t    with connections() as (ledger, _items, index):\n    62\t        if not ARGS.lexical:\n    63\t            try:\n    64\t                embedded, _unchanged, _tokens, error = search_module.ensure_index(ledger, index)\n    65\t                if error:\n    66\t                    sys.stderr.write(f'hivemind: embedding stopped ({error}) after {embedded} views; search runs lexical until the rest is built\\n')\n    67\t            except service.FirstDayNotCompleted:\n    68\t                sys.stderr.write(\"hivemind: index not built, the store's first day has not completed; search is lexical until a restart\\n\")\n    69\t        try:\n    70\t            day = service.resolve_bound(ledger, None)\n    71\t        except service.FirstDayNotCompleted:\n    72\t            return \"No day of this ledger has completed yet; every tool refuses until one has.\"\n    73\t        return (f'Objects as of {day}, when this server started; every tool reads the current last completed day. '\n    74\t                + idea_module.object_list(ledger, day, ALIASES))\n    75\t\n     4\tfamilies listed (4 against 2), which meets the rule's first half; its share of last judgements both families call supported is lower by 19\n     5\tpoints (10 of 15 against 6 of 7), more than the one in ten the second half allows. Each half has one named cause. The first is one rule: the\n     6\tthree matters the clean path lacks are the company's own revenue and margin, which its request forbids as questions (D382). The second rests\n     7\tmostly on one reader family: Codex failed 2 of the 4 judgements a separate reader had confirmed as supported, both of them production's;\n     8\tboth families call only one judgement unsupported, production's data-center revenue.\n     9\t\n    10\tMaterial: 2026-09-22..28, 235 articles (232 never sent by any run), each system one draw from an empty library: the clean path\n    11\t`poc/data/clean-lean-week-2026-11-14/week-r2/c1` (after D488), production `…/week/p1`. Readers: Codex (read-only) and Claude subagents, blind\n    12\tto the systems and to each other; the keys are outside the repository. Model cost of the step (the one-day slice, production's draw, the\n    13\tclean draw and its two stopped attempts): $4.69. One draw each: every count below is one draw.\n    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n   132\t        for key in totals:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '7047,7075p;9293,9322p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '79,105p'; rg -n '\"'^def library|''^def .*bundle|class'\"' src/hivemind/bundle.py | tail -22; nl -ba poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/replay.log | tail -4; rg -n '09-21|09-27|10-27' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -18 | cut -c1-300\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '7047,7075p;9293,9322p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '79,105p'; rg -n '\"'^def library|''^def .*bundle|class'\"' src/hivemind/bundle.py | tail -22; nl -ba poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/replay.log | tail -4; rg -n '09-21|09-27|10-27' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -18 | cut -c1-300\"","aggregated_output":"  7047\t## D560 · 2026-11-15 · Reflection council (Alex's request): the goal, the measuring method and the way through; a pilot of Alex's own product-level review is prepared at $0; the role of the six lines is put to him (council consensus)\n  7048\t\n  7049\t- **Alex** (2026-11-15): \"我觉得你的council 需要认真的end to end read 我现在的system design, 以及过去所有的尝试，到底你要达到的目标是什么？是不是量测方法问题，\n  7050\t  我们已经stuck 很久了需要重新审视突破\".\n  7051\t- **Council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-4/`): my own reflection written first (`own-reflection.md`); five\n  7052\t  cold reads with no position given: the goal and the design (`codex-design.md`), every past attempt (`codex-history.md`,\n  7053\t  incomplete by its own account; `claude-history.md`, every index row from D229 to D559 and the round logs), the measuring\n  7054\t  method (`codex-measurement.md`, `claude-measurement.md`); two challenge rounds (`council-codex-2.md`: no; `council-codex-3.md`:\n  7055\t  \"CONSENSUS: yes\").\n  7056\t- **The agreed answers.**\n  7057\t  1. *The goal:* a continuing research library in which an analyst finds the important questions, the facts for and against,\n  7058\t     and a present answer whose reasons are visible (PRD 00, Purpose; `clean-arch/PRD.md` §1; PRD 10 §1). The record carries\n  7059\t     four goals at once (PRD 10 §1; \"beats the old system\", D427; the six lines for answer choices, D400; use on unseen\n  7060\t     news, D484, its lines proposed) and no single number for \"ready\".\n  7061\t  2. *The measuring method:* a major part of the impasse, beside demonstrated product defects; the present sticks cannot\n  7062\t     apportion the two. The first gate has substantial reader disagreement, nothing on record clears it, and no measured\n  7063\t     link to the final answer; the July end-to-end reference could not rank the systems at that size and under that\n  7064\t     matching rule; the conditions measured were not the product's.\n  7065\t  3. *Why stuck, and the way through:* too many local pass-or-fail decisions with no reliable link to what the analyst sees,\n  7066\t     while important facts and answerable questions still go missing. First a small, source-backed review of actual answers\n  7067\t     by Alex himself, as a pilot; then the real starting-library condition (D559's comparison); product work chosen from\n  7068\t     what those two show.\n  7069\t- **Verified first-hand for this record.**\n  7070\t  - The first gate's instrument: one reader family holds every firm mark on 47 of 111 answer-choice lists, the other on 84;\n  7071\t    of the 36 lists the old system wrote for other questions, two readers held every firm mark on 19 and on 25,\n  7072\t    unadjudicated (`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/result/RESULT.md`); \"sound ladders given a failed mark: 3 of 7 | 0 of 7\"\n  7073\t    (`DESIGN.md`). A warning that nothing on record clears the whole gate, not a proof that nothing can. Seven readings, no\n  7074\t    pass.\n  7075\t  - D400's six lines were Claude's proposal (\"通过线我提议 …\"), accepted by Alex as the recommended option, with no chance\n  9293\t## D662 · 2026-11-17 · Reflection council 9 (Alex's request): the work drifted from D560's agreed way out; hold the listed work and put Deck 1 to Alex first (council consensus)\n  9294\t\n  9295\t- **Alex** (2026-11-17), sharing a critique (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-9/alex-critique-2026-11-17.md`, with Claude's check of\n  9296\t  its numbers): \"你看一下这个，我觉得你完全drift 了。你到底要怎么回归正轨来解决问题，深度的review traces然后跑council loop skill 直到你有确切的解决方案\".\n  9297\t- **Council** (`reflection-9/`):\n  9298\t  - Claude's own reflection, written first (`own-reflection.md`);\n  9299\t  - two cold readings made apart: a fresh Codex session with its memories off (`cold-codex-1.md`, thread 01a1ebfe-4f67-7c72-af87-7830055e0f09) and\n  9300\t    a Claude-family reviewer (`cold-claude-1.md`);\n  9301\t  - two challenge rounds (`codex-challenge-1.md`: disagree, with corrections; `codex-challenge-2.md`: \"CONSENSUS\").\n  9302\t- **Agreed reading:**\n  9303\t  - **No finish line.** The product goal has no finish line in numbers that Alex owns. Gate 3's \"beats\" has no number, gate 4's lines are\n  9304\t    proposed, gate 5 is unwritten, and D544's \"bound agreed later\" was never agreed.\n  9305\t  - **The work circled.** The next task kept being chosen from the nearest failed check, while D560 had found that the first gate has no measured\n  9306\t    link to the final answer. D623 had recorded that its zero-fault lines were a poor target on the luna-era readings.\n  9307\t  - **Engineering for later gates** ran while gate 1 failed (the live store D593–D603, the planner and integration), against \"nothing later in\n  9308\t    the plan … starts before it passes\" and D509's scope.\n  9309\t  - **The way out D560 agreed was dropped.** That way out was Alex's own half hour on Deck 1, then the comparison design, then the six lines'\n  9310\t    role. The deck was built on 11-15 and \"goes to him unchanged\" through D581, then vanished from the reports. Reflection 8 did not read D560.\n  9311\t    That is the fifth miss of the search-earlier-traces rule.\n  9312\t- **Corrected in this round:**\n  9313\t  - D656's share-control rule was written before the send, so its FAIL stands, beside the finding that the edit recovered 9 of 9 targets while\n  9314\t    the listing omission is in both arms.\n  9315\t  - D623's rates are luna-era, not astra's chance.\n  9316\t  - Four model switches were Alex's requests, and D544 stated its reasons.\n  9317\t  - The page fix for completed replays addressed a real defect.\n  9318\t- **Decided (consensus; D439's limits):**\n  9319\t  1. **Held while Alex's marks are pending,** with records kept:\n  9320\t     - answer-choice changes and D656's listing census;\n  9321\t     - model trials;\n  9322\t     - further live-store, planner and integration work.\n    79\t   - the archived runs in `docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md`.\n    80\t\n    81\t   Search goes inside binary files (`rg -a`, and SQL over every SQLite table for the ids). Its controls:\n    82\t   - a known hit: one of D613's 10 Step 1 reads in the week of 09-07;\n    83\t   - a known miss: one id written only into a scratch control file outside the searched roots.\n    84\t4. **Any read excludes the article, with one exception by actual use,** classified per folder and frozen before any hit is read:\n    85\t   - **The exception:** an old-system replay run folder and its byte copies, **only when** its decision record or run note shows it ran the\n    86\t     then-production configuration as the product (its library sealed or served as the product's), and no decision cites one of its articles as a\n    87\t     case behind a change.\n    88\t   - **Development replays are reads:** arms, probes, configuration trials and week tests.\n    89\t   - **Why:** a replay of the product as it ran tunes neither system. D665's own council used the sealed run as the old system's output.\n    90\t   - **Still a read:** any research artifact built from such a run (for example, the 2026-10-28 quality review).\n    91\t   - **Recorded:** the per-folder classification (`replay-folders.json`, with each folder's record) and the council decision on it, both before\n    92\t     the hits are read.\n    93\t5. **One input.**\n    94\t   - A filtered copy of the items database without the excluded articles is made once and hashed.\n    95\t   - **Code change A:** `run_fresh.py --items` hands it to both children (clean `--source`; production `--testdb`).\n    96\t   - **Code change B:** `fresh_week_inputs.py` takes the dates and the items path as arguments.\n    97\t   - **Proof through the real entry points:** both launchers run dry with fake answers over the whole span on the copy. Each records the\n    98\t     ordered ids it actually processes and their text sha. The two must be equal in order. Controls:\n    99\t     - an excluded article appears in neither;\n   100\t     - a kept article appears in both.\n   101\t\n   102\t### 1.3 Blind matter census (articles only; frozen before any send)\n   103\t\n   104\t1. **Sample (D668).** Every kept article in the scored window 2026-08-31 to 09-20, read in batches of about 40 per session. Each family merges across every batch and week before reconciling. The warm-up is 07-01 to 08-30, unfiltered: the exclusion filter applies to the scored window only. Read with week reading A1's\n   105\t   brief (`../2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A1.md`), unchanged except for the file names.\n100:def view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\n183:def _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\n219:def thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\n225:def library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n    82\t2026-09-19 | items  34 extracted  29 merged  5 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  58 new views  1 judged  37 changed  18 closed 0 | open views 42 | day $0.12 total $6.60 calls 8630\n    83\t2026-09-20 | items  34 extracted  28 merged  6 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence  39 new views  1 judged  36 changed  20 closed 1 | open views 42 | day $0.12 total $6.72 calls 8737\n    84\ttotals: {'items': 2077, 'extracted': 1884, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 193, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0, 'evidence': 5120, 'new_views': 43, 'judged': 1616, 'changed': 882, 'closed': 1}\n    85\tledger: {'ceiling': 25.0, 'spent': 8.59927935400001, 'reserved': 5.100087019371813e-16, 'overrun': False, 'refused': 0, 'attempts': 8737, 'stopped': False, 'stop_reason': None, 'launchers': {'old-2': '/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/launch.lock'}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-claude.md:47:**Recommendation and one test.** Run poc-v118 forward from one old draw's 09-20 store over the unseen 09-21..10-27 articles (already\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-round2-brief.md:25:   copy) with its alerts. Its first week runs forward from that 09-20 store over the already harvested 09-21..09-27, as a dress\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-round2-brief.md:31:- (b) Is the rehearsal week on harvested articles a sound first pilot, given that the corpus stops at 10-27 and the feed is unbuilt?\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p2-codex.stream:9:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-claude.md | head -130; rg -n 'D560|D606|D358|D424' d\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p2-codex.stream:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '177,219p;240,310p'; nl -ba scripts/hivemind\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n '\\\"'^(#|.*D(563|66[5-9]|67[0-9]|68[0-9]|690))|refusal|production'\\\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; nl -ba README.md;\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md; nl -ba docs/poc/service.md; nl -\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n '\\\"'^#|D563|D665|D689|D690'\\\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n 'replay|service|MCP|Idea|upstream|daily|Jev|conf\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:28:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/FINDINGS.md | head -155; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-ac\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:34:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_17\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,538p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10308,10375p'; ls -l poc/\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:42:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ls -lh poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/ledgers/old* poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod; nl -ba poc/d\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:44:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"head -3 poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/ledgers/old-1.attempts.jsonl | cut -c1-450; nl -ba scripts/cost_report.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:47:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md | sed -n '348,396p;583,640p'; nl\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:53:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_27\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3673,3720p;4787,4828p;4962,5006p'; rg -n '\\\"'^(#|.*must-open|.*judgement|.*\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:57:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_29\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '62,162p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '51,143p'; nl -ba sr\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:71:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_36\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop | rg 'proof-v108|frozen-v108' | head -40; rg -n 'v74i|poc-v108' docs/\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:73:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md | sed -n '49,76p;97,108p'; nl -ba docs/research\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/council-p-codex.stream:75:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n '\\\"'^## D(665|668|672|676|677)'\\\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '\\\"'^## |''^'\\\"\\\\\\\\|.*prod' docs/research/20\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport collections,json,pathlib,sqlite3\np=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\nfor name in (\\\"old-1\\\",\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"old-3\\\"):\n  rec=json.loads((p/name/\\\"run.json\\\").read_text())\n  assert rec[\\\"state\\\"]==\\\"complete\\\"\n  path=p/name/\\\"prod/archive.sqlite\\\"\n  assert not any(path.with_name(path.name+s).exists() for s in (\\\"-wal\\\",\\\"-shm\\\",\\\"-journal\\\"))\n  with sqlite3.connect(path.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True) as c:\n    sums=collections.defaultdict(float)\n    counts=collections.Counter()\n    for model,i,o,cache in c.execute(\\\"select model,input_tokens,output_tokens,case when json_valid(response_json) then coalesce(json_extract(response_json,'\\\\''\"'$.usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens'\"'\\\\''),0) else 0 end from model_calls\\\"):\n      k=\\\"jev\\\" if model==\\\"jev-1.14.0\\\" else \\\"llm\\\"\n      i,o=i or 0,o or 0\n      sums[k]+=(i*.042 if k==\\\"jev\\\" else (i-min(i,cache))*.10+min(i,cache)*.01+o*.50)/1e6\n      counts[k]+=1\n  attempts=collections.Counter()\n  charges=collections.defaultdict(float)\n  jev_tokens=0\n  no_usage=collections.Counter()\n  for line in (p/\\\"ledgers\\\"/(name+\\\".attempts.jsonl\\\")).open():\n    a=json.loads(line)\n    k=a[\\\"kind\\\"]\n    attempts[k]+=1\n    charges[k]+=a.get(\\\"charged\\\",0)\n    if k==\\\"jev\\\": jev_tokens+=a.get(\\\"tokens\\\") or 0\n    if a.get(\\\"charged\\\")==a.get(\\\"reserved\\\"): no_usage[k]+=1\n  state=json.loads((p/\\\"ledgers\\\"/(name+\\\".json\\\")).read_text())\n  print(name,\\\"calls\\\",dict(counts),\\\"attempts\\\",dict(attempts),\\\"priced\\\",dict(sums),\\\"guard booked\\\",dict(charges),\\\"gap jev\\\",charges[\\\"jev\\\"]-sums[\\\"jev\\\"],\\\"gap llm\\\",charges[\\\"llm\\\"]-sums[\\\"llm\\\"],\\\"jev token single price\\\",jev_tokens*.042/1e6,\\\"settled at reservation\\\",dict(no_usage),\\\"balance\\\",state[\\\"reserved\\\"])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
