ettled at reservation\\\",dict(no_usage),\\\"balance\\\",state[\\\"reserved\\\"])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1 calls {'llm': 3561, 'jev': 5469} attempts {'llm': 3562, 'jev': 5469} priced {'llm': 6.196088039999999, 'jev': 1.2057892979999951} guard booked {'llm': 6.21606364, 'jev': 3.617367894000001} gap jev 2.411578596000006 gap llm 0.019975600000000426 jev token single price 1.2057892980000002 settled at reservation {'llm': 1} balance 2.1163626406917047e-16\nold-2 calls {'llm': 3574, 'jev': 5163} attempts {'llm': 3574, 'jev': 5163} priced {'llm': 5.778472750000002, 'jev': 0.940268868} guard booked {'llm': 5.778472750000003, 'jev': 2.8208066040000026} gap jev 1.8805377360000026 gap llm 8.881784197001252e-16 jev token single price 0.940268868 settled at reservation {} balance 5.100087019371813e-16\nold-3 calls {'llm': 3666, 'jev': 5517} attempts {'llm': 3666, 'jev': 5517} priced {'llm': 5.854836179999994, 'jev': 0.9906918000000035} guard booked {'llm': 5.854836179999994, 'jev': 2.9720754000000005} gap jev 1.981383599999997 gap llm 0.0 jev token single price 0.9906918 settled at reservation {} balance 6.036837696399289e-16\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '1,39p;175,242p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '15,82p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/testdb.py | sed -n '1,115p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '9318,9336p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_inputs.py | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '1,39p;175,242p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '15,82p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/testdb.py | sed -n '1,115p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '9318,9336p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_inputs.py | head -25\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\n     2\tevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\n     3\tswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\n     4\tend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\"\"\"\n     5\timport json\n     6\tfrom contextlib import contextmanager\n     7\tfrom datetime import date\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom . import service\n    10\tfrom .views import store\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t@contextmanager\n    14\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\n    15\t    \"\"\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\"\"\"\n    16\t    owned = []\n    17\t    try:\n    18\t        for conn in connections:\n    19\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\n    20\t                conn.execute('begin')\n    21\t                owned.append(conn)\n    22\t        yield\n    23\t    finally:\n    24\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\n    25\t            conn.rollback()\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\n    29\t    \"\"\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\n    30\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\"\"\"\n    31\t    cache = {}\n    32\t\n    33\t    def item_of(input_id):\n    34\t        if input_id not in cache:\n    35\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\n    36\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\n    37\t        return cache[input_id]\n    38\t    return item_of\n    39\t\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\tdef days(views_db, as_of=None):\n   178\t    \"\"\"The completed days the front end's time axis runs over, up to as_of.\"\"\"\n   179\t    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\n   180\t    return [r[0] for r in views_db.execute('select day from days_completed order by day') if as_of is None or r[0] <= as_of]\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\tdef _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None, coverage='selection'):\n   184\t    \"\"\"Complete, dated UI inputs for caller-selected theses; no search, model call or ledger write. Its bound is already resolved\n   185\t    by its caller (`thesis_bundles`, `library`).\"\"\"\n   186\t    date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   187\t    if not isinstance(view_ids, list) or not view_ids or any(not isinstance(id, str) or not id for id in view_ids):\n   188\t        raise ValueError('thesis_bundles needs a non-empty list of view ids')\n   189\t    lookup = item_lookup(items_db)\n   190\t    records = []\n   191\t    for view_id in dict.fromkeys(view_ids):\n   192\t        row = views_db.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   193\t        if row is None or not service.view_exists(views_db, row, as_of):\n   194\t            raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\n   195\t        records.append(view_bundle(views_db, lookup, view_id, as_of))\n   196\t    return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': records,\n   197\t            'coverage': coverage, 'groups': research_groups(views_db, view_ids, as_of)}\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\tdef research_groups(conn, view_ids, as_of):\n   201\t    \"\"\"Stored groups, with dated memberships limited to the envelope's loaded theses.\"\"\"\n   202\t    if not conn.execute('pragma table_info(thesis_groups)').fetchone():\n   203\t        return []\n   204\t    loaded = set(view_ids)\n   205\t    result = []\n   206\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from thesis_groups order by created_seq, rowid'):\n   207\t        if not service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of):\n   208\t            continue\n   209\t        members = [{'thesis_id': m['view_id'], 'day': service.day_of_seq(conn, m['seq']), 'basis': m['basis'] or ''}\n   210\t                   for m in conn.execute('select * from thesis_group_members where group_id=? order by id', (row['group_id'],))\n   211\t                   if m['view_id'] in loaded and service.visible(conn, m['seq'], as_of)]\n   212\t        if members:\n   213\t            result.append({'id': row['group_id'], 'name': row['name'], 'scope': row['scope'],\n   214\t                           'aliases': json.loads(row['aliases'] or '[]') if 'aliases' in row.keys() else [],\n   215\t                           'created_day': service.day_of_seq(conn, row['created_seq']), 'members': members})\n   216\t    return result\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\tdef thesis_bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of=None):\n   220\t    \"\"\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\"\"\"\n   221\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   222\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n   226\t    \"\"\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\"\"\"\n   227\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   228\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n   229\t        if not as_of:\n   230\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\n   231\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   232\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\n   233\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\n   234\t        if not view_ids:\n   235\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\n   236\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\n    15\tTIER_FACT = vocabulary.TIERS[0]          # 'fact'; a legacy ledger's '发生的事' compares equal through vocabulary.canonical\n    16\tCOMPARATORS = ('>=', '<', '=')\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef open_ledger(path):\n    20\t    \"\"\"A read-only connection to a views database.\"\"\"\n    21\t    return store.open_read_only(path)\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\tdef default_as_of(conn):\n    25\t    \"\"\"Today's default day: the last completed day, or a legacy ledger's last judgement day. Read only through `resolve_bound`.\"\"\"\n    26\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) or conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from judgements').fetchone()[0]\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tclass FirstDayNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    30\t    \"\"\"The store holds processing steps and no completed day: its first day is still in progress, and nothing is served from it\n    31\t    (live-service/OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 4; open defect 10).\"\"\"\n    32\t\n    33\t    def __init__(self):\n    34\t        super().__init__(\"the store's first day has not completed\")\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tclass BoundNotCompleted(ValueError):\n    38\t    \"\"\"An explicit upper bound later than the store's last completed day: refused, naming that day (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\"\"\"\n    39\t\n    40\t    def __init__(self, requested, last_completed_day):\n    41\t        self.requested, self.last_completed_day = requested, last_completed_day\n    42\t        super().__init__(f'day not completed: {requested} is after the last completed day {last_completed_day}')\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tclass RangeNotOrdered(ValueError):\n    46\t    \"\"\"A range whose start is after its resolved end: a window reaching into days not yet completed (council round 124).\"\"\"\n    47\t\n    48\t    def __init__(self, start, end):\n    49\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\n    50\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    54\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\n    59\t\n    60\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\n    61\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\n    62\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\n    63\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\"\"\"\n    64\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    65\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\n    66\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    67\t    if not bound:\n    68\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\n    69\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\n    70\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\n    71\t    return bound\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\n    75\t    \"\"\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\n    76\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\n    77\t    start is included; a client polling \"what changed since the day I last saw\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\n    78\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\"\"\"\n    79\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\n    80\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\n    81\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\n    82\t    return end\n     1\t\"\"\"The test database: the corpus items.sqlite built by poc/corpus/scripts/assemble.py, read as a stream in\n     2\tpublication order. This is \"the team's own database\" of D7: the system keeps no copy of the material, only the\n     3\tprocessing record; an item's text is read from here when it is processed.\n     4\t\n     5\tOrder inside a day (the arrival order upstream would give): company documents (filings, transcripts, releases),\n     6\tofficial material, then news by published_at. Only items with feed = 1 (an original, whole) or a copy of one are\n     7\tstreamed; the rest stay in the database for the review.\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport sqlite3\n    11\t\n    12\tdef open_db(path):\n    13\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\n    14\t    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    15\t    return conn\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\tdef feed(conn, from_day, until_day):\n    19\t    \"\"\"Yield items with from_day <= publication_day <= until_day in processing order.\"\"\"\n    20\t    rows = conn.execute(\n    21\t        \"select * from items where publication_day >= ? and publication_day <= ? and (feed = 1 or copy_of is not null) \"\n    22\t        \"order by publication_day, case klass when '公司材料' then 0 when '官方材料' then 1 else 2 end, \"\n    23\t        \"coalesce(published_at, ''), rowid\", (from_day, until_day))\n    24\t    for row in rows:\n    25\t        yield item_of(row)\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef item_of(row):\n    29\t    \"\"\"A stored row as the item the pipeline reads: its object identifiers parsed.\"\"\"\n    30\t    item = dict(row)\n    31\t    item['object_identifiers'] = json.loads(item.get('object_identifiers') or '[]')\n    32\t    return item\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef count(conn, from_day, until_day):\n    36\t    return conn.execute(\"select count(*) from items where publication_day >= ? and publication_day <= ? and feed = 1\", (from_day, until_day)).fetchone()[0]\n  9318\t- **Decided (consensus; D439's limits):**\n  9319\t  1. **Held while Alex's marks are pending,** with records kept:\n  9320\t     - answer-choice changes and D656's listing census;\n  9321\t     - model trials;\n  9322\t     - further live-store, planner and integration work.\n  9323\t\n  9324\t     D658 is not held by this decision. Alex is asked separately whether it may wait until his marks.\n  9325\t  2. **First: Deck 1, unchanged** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/deck-1.html`). It answers only \"enough to design the next\n  9326\t     comparison?\"\n  9327\t     - **Yes** if he marks the full deck within 45 minutes (30 is the target), rejects both planted wrong answers, accepts the supported control,\n  9328\t       and matches both marks on at least 2 of 3 repeats.\n  9329\t     - **Anything unmet** (a skipped control or \"cannot tell\" included) is inspected for its cause before the method is relied on.\n  9330\t     - **Reported either way:** every real-card disagreement with his reasons, whether he opened the full material, the three missing-fact\n  9331\t       sheets and the time.\n  9332\t     - **It does not decide** a system, assess astra's output, or change a reader family's role in a gate.\n  9333\t  3. **Questions for Alex, in order:**\n  9334\t     - **Today:** will he mark the deck, and may D658 wait until his marks (recommended yes to both)? If the reference is to continue, he\n  9335\t       chooses between completing the approved luna-question reference and a separately reviewed design for astra's questions.\n  9336\t     - **After the deck:** should the six lines still block release, or be reported while readiness is decided by a controlled comparison of\nnl: docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_inputs.py: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,\\\"src\\\")\nfrom hivemind import bundle, testdb\nbase=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\\\")\nassert json.loads((base/\\\"run/old-2/run.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"state\\\"]==\\\"complete\\\"\ndef ro(p):\n  assert not any(p.with_name(p.name+s).exists() for s in (\\\"-wal\\\",\\\"-shm\\\",\\\"-journal\\\"))\n  c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n  c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n  return c\nwith ro(base/\\\"run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\\") as ledger, ro(base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") as items:\n  data=bundle.library(ledger,items)\n  print(\\\"same shared bundle, date, open by switch summary, all, groups\\\",data[\\\"as_of\\\"],len(data[\\\"views\\\"]),len(data[\\\"groups\\\"]),len(data[\\\"days\\\"]))\n  print(\\\"shape\\\",list(data[\\\"views\\\"][0]),\\\"same explicit date\\\",data==bundle.library(ledger,items,\\\"2026-09-20\\\"))\n  print(\\\"comparison db September 21-27 items\\\",sum(1 for _ in testdb.feed(items,\\\"2026-09-21\\\",\\\"2026-09-27\\\")))\nwith ro(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")) as items:\n  from collections import Counter\n  print(\\\"original corpus September 21-27 daily feed counts\\\",Counter(x[\\\"publication_day\\\"] for x in testdb.feed(items,\\\"2026-09-21\\\",\\\"2026-09-27\\\")))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib,sqlite3,sys\nsys.path.insert(0,\\\"src\\\")\nfrom hivemind import bundle, testdb\nbase=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\\\")\nassert json.loads((base/\\\"run/old-2/run.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"state\\\"]==\\\"complete\\\"\ndef ro(p):\n  assert not any(p.with_name(p.name+s).exists() for s in (\\\"-wal\\\",\\\"-shm\\\",\\\"-journal\\\"))\n  c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n  c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n  return c\nwith ro(base/\\\"run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\\") as ledger, ro(base/\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\") as items:\n  data=bundle.library(ledger,items)\n  print(\\\"same shared bundle, date, open by switch summary, all, groups\\\",data[\\\"as_of\\\"],len(data[\\\"views\\\"]),len(data[\\\"groups\\\"]),len(data[\\\"days\\\"]))\n  print(\\\"shape\\\",list(data[\\\"views\\\"][0]),\\\"same explicit date\\\",data==bundle.library(ledger,items,\\\"2026-09-20\\\"))\n  print(\\\"comparison db September 21-27 items\\\",sum(1 for _ in testdb.feed(items,\\\"2026-09-21\\\",\\\"2026-09-27\\\")))\nwith ro(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\")) as items:\n  from collections import Counter\n  print(\\\"original corpus September 21-27 daily feed counts\\\",Counter(x[\\\"publication_day\\\"] for x in testdb.feed(items,\\\"2026-09-21\\\",\\\"2026-09-27\\\")))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"same shared bundle, date, open by switch summary, all, groups 2026-09-20 43 26 82\nshape ['view_id', 'object', 'kind', 'looks_at', 'question', 'due_day', 'year', 'identity', 'successions', 'created_seq', 'created_day', 'created_from', 'rungs', 'open', 'switches', 'judgements', 'evidence', 'dependencies', 'dependants', 'not_judged', 'answer_shape', 'favourable_end'] same explicit date True\ncomparison db September 21-27 items 567\noriginal corpus September 21-27 daily feed counts Counter({'2026-09-21': 110, '2026-09-24': 100, '2026-09-25': 87, '2026-09-22': 82, '2026-09-23': 79, '2026-09-27': 67, '2026-09-26': 42})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"**Show Alex v118’s output before building the daily feed.** A half-hour with the September 20 library can answer whether he would use it and whether a week-long rehearsal is worth funding. [D560](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:7056)\n\n**Cost.** I repriced the completed archives from tokens at the repository rates. The three 82-day draws came to **$7.40, $6.72 and $6.85**. The guard booked **$9.83, $8.60 and $8.83** because it charges three attempts’ worth of tokens for every Jev response, adding $2.41, $1.88 and $1.98. Draw 1 also booked $0.02 for one extra Luna attempt at its reservation. No meaningful reservation balance remained. Tell Alex **$6.72–$7.40 in recorded model usage, with $8.60–$9.83 booked against the spending guard**. [Token pricing](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/cost_report.py:17) · [Guard accounting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:268)\n\n**(a) Yes.** I ran the shared library reader directly against the finished old-2 files. It returned September 20 and all 43 questions, including 42 open. For the $0 review, pair the ledger with its matching articles, verify that the page, API and MCP show the same day and source links, and confirm the page fetched the library. It silently keeps the embedded v34 copy if the fetch fails. Use the default latest-day view and let Alex follow citations. This checks browsing and analyst usefulness. Idea calls and daily updates remain untested. [Shared reader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:225) · [Page fallback](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254) · [Local serving](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/README.md:118)\n\n**(b) Yes, as a rehearsal.** If Alex sees value, advance a copy one day at a time over September 21–27, publish each completed day, and simulate one failed day to verify the alert and last-good copy. The articles exist and the replay can continue from September 20. Some of that week was already used in research. Live arrival, late articles and the gap after October 27 still need an explicit plan before switching to today. [Replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:51) · [Prior week test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md:10)\n\n**(c) Disclose both results.** They justify asking Alex whether missing questions and weak answers undermine usefulness. They leave room for a private test of exactly that. [Release diagnostic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md:124) · [July census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/CENSUS-FULL-RESULT.md:21)\n\n**CONSENSUS**"}}
